sub:assertion {
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/darwin1859-ch13-11> delphi:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/darwin1859-ch13-11--grok> .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/darwin1859-ch13-11--grok> a delphi:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Grok 4.7 on darwin1859-ch13-11: partially-resolvable, resolvability 0.55" ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/dataset-resolvability-0.1.0> ;
    delphi:assessmentType "dataset-resolvability/0.1.0" ;
    delphi:hasScore "0.548"^^xsd:double ;
    delphi:hasVerdict "partially-resolvable" ;
    delphi:hasConfidence "0.54"^^xsd:double ;
    dct:description "Character mapping can separate a general resemblance to a group from a special resemblance to one species, which is the empirical contrast in the sentence. The required matrices exist for scattered taxa rather than for every cross-group affinity Darwin had in mind. Months of character coding would still leave a moderate risk that the result restates how the characters were chosen." ;
    rdfs:comment "Proposed test with existing data: When a species shares characters with a distant group, map those characters on an independent tree and ask whether they are ancestral for the distant group or shared uniquely with one of its species. The claim is confirmed if such cross-group similarities are usually general plesiomorphies, and refuted if they usually match derived characters of a single species." ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-resolvability-assessor-grok-4.7-high-fast> ;
    delphi:evidenceAgainst "Pre-cladistic 'affinity' mixes ancestral resemblance with convergence, so the characters to map are not uniquely defined.", "Many matrices were assembled in order to resolve these same affinities, which makes the mapping partly circular.", "The living members of a group are an incomplete sample of the ancient parent group whose characters the claim invokes." ;
    delphi:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/darwin1859-ch13-11--grok--dataset-1>, <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/darwin1859-ch13-11--grok--dataset-2>, <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/darwin1859-ch13-11--grok--dataset-3> .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/darwin1859-ch13-11--grok--operationalizability> a delphi:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Operationalizability of darwin1859-ch13-11 by Grok 4.7: 0.55" ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/dataset-resolvability-0.1.0-operationalizability> ;
    delphi:assessmentType "dataset-resolvability/0.1.0/operationalizability" ;
    delphi:hasScore "0.55"^^xsd:double ;
    dct:isPartOf <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/darwin1859-ch13-11--grok> ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-resolvability-assessor-grok-4.7-high-fast> .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/darwin1859-ch13-11> delphi:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/darwin1859-ch13-11--grok--operationalizability> .
